{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>At the mouth of Aharon and his sons shall be all the service of the sons of the Gershonite</b> – Now which of the sons is appointed over them? Itamar, in the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 4:27). But this is not correct, for why would it mention Aharon? Rather, the meaning of <b>at the mouth of Aharon and his sons it shall be</b> is that their service shall be at their command: they shall appoint the sons of the Gershonite to their service. They shall say: So-and-so of the sons of Gershon shall be the treasurer over such-and-such a matter, and so-and-so shall be the singer or the gatekeeper for such-and-such, and so-and-so shall carry from the curtains such-and-such. And also on the journey they shall not dismantle nor load until Aharon and his sons command them. Now all of them require supervision, which is the appointment, and Elazar is overseer over all three princes, and Itamar is treasurer over Gershon and Merari. And it says, \"and you shall appoint them in charge of their charge,\" for Moshe shall be with them at the time of appointment when they assign the watches to them, but in the hand of Itamar shall be their charge, for each one shall return his vessels to his hand at the encampments of the Mishkan and say to him: 'Behold, before you are the vessels entrusted to my hand.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:02:40.126905579Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}